{"problem":"How many different ordered triples (a, b, c) of non-negative integers are there such that a+b+c=99?","reference_answer":"5050","reference_solution":"For any c, we know that a+b=99-c.
Thus, there are 99-c+1 different values of (a, b), ranging from (0, 99-c) to (99-c, 0).
